1. Install visual studio
2. Use the following command to compile .c code to .dll file

2.1 For 32 bit build, first initialize with this command(fill ****with your VS code installation location or find path for "vcvarsall.bat"):

"<****\Microsoft Visual Studio\2022\Community\VC\Auxiliary\Build\vcvarsall.bat>" x86

2.2 Then run:

cl .\src\GFM_GFL_IBR.c /I .\inc /LD /link /OUT:GFM_GFL_IBR_X86.dll

2.3 For 64 bit build, first initialize:

"<****\Microsoft Visual Studio\2022\Community\VC\Auxiliary\Build\vcvarsall.bat>" x64

2.4 Then run:

cl .\src\GFM_GFL_IBR.c /I .\inc /LD /link /OUT:GFM_GFL_IBR_X64.dll

3. Put .dll files under Library folder 

